            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nice3"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this drink! Used Cointreau instead of Triiple Sec and Sprite Zero for the lemon-lime soda. Did not rim the glasses with salt. Will definitely be making it again. Thanks for sharing your recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KZrod"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been a bartender/bar-manager for over 20 years. This Margarita was yummy!! I used espalone tequila and I freshly squeezed two limes instead or using the Rose's lime. That is the only change I made other then I NEVER shake anything carbonated EVER. That is a disaster I prefer to avoid. I got all my ingredients set in the shaker (minus the seltzer), added ice, shook, poured over fresh ice, and topped it off with the seltzer. Ive made that mistake many a times in my years.... i just find it better to avoid the explosion. lol",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-07T19:43:12.790Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CookingWithShelia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I enjoyed the freshness that came from the lemon-lime soda. I did make the following changes:\n\n1. I used fresh squeezed lime juice vs. rose's lime.\n2. Agave vs. Triple Sec\n3. No ice.\n4. Topped with lemon lime soda vs. shaking it in the shaker.",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-30T19:54:54.170Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Wramos"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing! Tasted just like our fav marg from the chain restaurant we often visit. The only thing I did different was add a equal packet to some fresh squeezed lime juice instead of using the sweetend lime juice from the bottle you get at the store. Seemed kind of silly not to just use fresh. Very yummy!! We were drinking these all Cinco De Mayo weekend!!!",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-09T08:39:35.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chriskitten8"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I actually multiplied this recipe to make 16 servings and pre-made it in a giant pitcher for a football party, then just poured it into ice filled glasses. I used Diet 7-Up and frozen limeade concentrate, which I mixed with 4 cans of water before using for the margaritas. It's very refreshing and light, and sure packs a punch! It makes a strong drink, but that's how I like it! I live in Arizona, so I went to the backyard and pulled limes off my tree and squeezed a fresh lime into each glass, YUM!",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-24T13:16:27.010Z"
          },
